# 10. Improvements you should consider in production

This starter is intentionally simple. In production, I’d strongly recommend:

## A. Better conflict resolution
Current strategy:
- client keeps pending local changes
- server uses last-write-wins

Better options:
- field-level merges
- version numbers
- server revision tokens
- manual conflict review UI

## B. Batch sync
Instead of sending one queue item at a time:

- POST `/api/surveys/sync/batch`
- send multiple queued changes
- reduce network overhead

## C. Authentication
Add:
- JWT or session auth
- encrypted local storage if sensitive
- per-user data partitioning

## D. Attachments/photos
For field surveying, photos are common:
- store blobs in IndexedDB
- upload separately
- retry failed uploads independently

## E. Background sync API
If supported, use:
- Service Worker Background Sync
- Periodic Background Sync

## F. Geolocation integration
Auto-fill coordinates:

```javascript
navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition(
  pos => {
    console.log(pos.coords.latitude, pos.coords.longitude);
  },
  err => {
    console.error(err);
  }
);
```

