# 1. Architecture

## Requirements covered

A field surveying app usually needs to:

- Create survey records offline
- Edit records offline
- Store photos / notes / coordinates locally
- Mark records as pending sync
- Detect when connectivity returns
- Push unsynced changes to server
- Pull latest server changes
- Resolve conflicts safely

## Offline-first pattern

Each survey record has:

- `id`: stable UUID
- `updatedAt`: local timestamp
- `serverUpdatedAt`: last known server timestamp
- `syncStatus`: `"pending" | "synced" | "failed"`
- `deleted`: soft delete flag
- `version`: incrementing version for conflict detection

