# 6. Better Conflict Strategy Example

Instead of only timestamps, use `version`.

Server can reject stale writes:

```javascript
app.post("/surveys/sync", (req, res) => {
  const incoming = req.body;
  const existing = surveys.get(incoming.id);

  if (!existing) {
    const saved = { ...incoming, serverUpdatedAt: new Date().toISOString() };
    surveys.set(incoming.id, saved);
    return res.json(saved);
  }

  if (incoming.version < existing.version) {
    return res.status(409).json({
      error: "Conflict",
      serverRecord: existing
    });
  }

  const saved = {
    ...existing,
    ...incoming,
    serverUpdatedAt: new Date().toISOString()
  };

  surveys.set(incoming.id, saved);
  res.json(saved);
});
```

Then frontend can handle `409 Conflict` and show a merge UI.

