## 7. `background.js`

This listens for matched rules and increments a session counter.

```javascript
chrome.runtime.onInstalled.addListener(async () => {
  const existing = await chrome.storage.local.get({
    blockingEnabled: true,
    blockedCount: 0
  });

  await chrome.storage.local.set(existing);

  if (!existing.blockingEnabled) {
    await chrome.declarativeNetRequest.updateEnabledRulesets({
      enableRulesetIds: [],
      disableRulesetIds: ["tracker_rules"]
    });
  }
});

chrome.declarativeNetRequest.onRuleMatchedDebug.addListener(async () => {
  const result = await chrome.storage.local.get({ blockedCount: 0 });
  await chrome.storage.local.set({ blockedCount: result.blockedCount + 1 });
});
```

