## If you want real streaming data

You can replace the simulated stream with something like:

```js
const socket = new WebSocket('wss://your-feed.example.com/stocks');

socket.onmessage = (event) => {
  const tick = JSON.parse(event.data);
  // tick example:
  // { timestamp, changes: { AAPL: 1.2, MSFT: -0.4, ... } }

  state.timestamps.push(tick.timestamp);

  symbols.forEach((symbol, i) => {
    state.data[i].push(tick.changes[symbol] ?? 0);
    if (state.data[i].length > state.maxHistory) state.data[i].shift();
  });

  if (state.timestamps.length > state.maxHistory) {
    state.timestamps.shift();
  }

  draw();
};
```

