# Optional upgraded backend reorder logic

The current reorder logic works for MVP use, but a safer version is:

```js
app.put("/api/projects/:projectId/reorder", (req, res) => {
  const project = getProject(req.params.projectId);
  if (!project) return res.status(404).json({ error: "Project not found" });

  const { taskId, sourceColumnId, destinationColumnId, destinationIndex } = req.body;

  const sourceColumn = project.columns.find((c) => c.id === sourceColumnId);
  const destinationColumn = project.columns.find((c) => c.id === destinationColumnId);

  if (!sourceColumn || !destinationColumn) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: "Invalid column IDs" });
  }

  sourceColumn.taskIds = sourceColumn.taskIds.filter((id) => id !== taskId);

  const safeIndex = Math.max(0, Math.min(destinationIndex, destinationColumn.taskIds.length));
  destinationColumn.taskIds.splice(safeIndex, 0, taskId);

  io.to(project.id).emit("task:moved", {
    projectId: project.id,
    taskId,
    sourceColumnId,
    destinationColumnId,
    destinationIndex: safeIndex
  });

  res.json({ success: true });
});
```

This avoids some index mismatch issues.

