# 3. Core principles for low latency

- Avoid unnecessary heap allocations in hot paths
- Prefer preallocated buffers
- Use bounded channels where possible
- Use CPU pinning for critical threads
- Keep market data and order routing on separate threads
- Use binary protocols internally if needed
- Minimize serialization on the hot path
- Batch noncritical writes to storage
- Persist asynchronously unless regulation/business requires sync durability

