# 8. How to make it truly low latency

## In-process optimizations
- use `ArrayQueue` or lock-free ring buffers
- preallocate objects/buffers
- use fixed-size structs where possible
- avoid `String` in hot path
- use integer timestamps
- avoid `chrono` in critical path
- use CPU affinity
- isolate GC if using Java; Rust avoids GC pauses

## Network/protocol optimizations
- kernel bypass only if truly needed and justified
- busy polling on dedicated cores
- NIC tuning
- huge pages if appropriate
- NUMA-aware thread placement

## Data structure optimizations
- use flat arrays instead of hash maps where possible
- instrument IDs mapped to compact indexes
- cache-friendly state layout

