# 2. Design principles for low latency

## Hot path rules
- Avoid heap allocations in critical loops
- Prefer preallocated buffers
- Avoid locks where possible
- Use bounded channels/ring buffers
- Keep data structures cache-friendly
- Minimize serialization/deserialization on hot path
- Pin threads/cores in production if needed
- Use binary protocols internally

## Scalability rules
- Partition by symbol/account/venue
- Make services stateless where possible
- Persist event streams for recovery
- Use clear interfaces so components can be replaced independently

