# Better scalable pattern: internal event bus

Instead of direct point-to-point channels everywhere, use an internal bus abstraction.

## Example bus interface

```rust
use common::Event;
use tokio::sync::broadcast;

#[derive(Clone)]
pub struct EventBus {
    tx: broadcast::Sender<Event>,
}

impl EventBus {
    pub fn new(capacity: usize) -> Self {
        let (tx, _) = broadcast::channel(capacity);
        Self { tx }
    }

    pub fn subscribe(&self) -> broadcast::Receiver<Event> {
        self.tx.subscribe()
    }

    pub fn publish(&self, event: Event) {
        let _ = self.tx.send(event);
    }
}
```

This makes it easier to:
- add more consumers
- split modules into separate processes later
- replace internal bus with NATS/Kafka later

For the absolute hottest path, you may later replace this with:
- lock-free ring buffers
- Aeron
- Disruptor-like patterns
- shared memory queues

