# 6. Critical low-latency path

The order lifecycle should look like this:

```text
Client
  -> Order Entry
  -> Basic validation
  -> Instrument partition routing
  -> Pre-trade risk check
  -> Sequence/journal event
  -> Matching engine
  -> Execution generation
  -> In-memory state update
  -> Ack/result to client
  -> Async publish to bus / persistence / analytics
```

## Important latency rules
- no synchronous SQL in this path
- no distributed transactions
- no cross-partition locks
- no blocking I/O
- use preallocated objects where possible
- avoid excessive GC pressure

