# 8. Sequencing and partitioning

To scale later, introduce **instrument partitioning** from the start.

## Partition strategy
```text
partition = hash(instrument) % N
```

Each partition has:
- One inbound queue
- One execution thread
- Its own order books
- Its own sequence numbers/journal

This allows future scaling by:
- Increasing partition count
- Moving partitions to separate processes/nodes

## Partition processor skeleton
```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public final class ExecutionPartition implements Runnable {
    private final BlockingQueue<Command> queue = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>();
    private final Map<String, OrderBook> books = new HashMap<>();
    private final IdGenerator orderIds;
    private final IdGenerator tradeIds;
    private volatile boolean running = true;

    public ExecutionPartition(IdGenerator orderIds, IdGenerator tradeIds) {
        this.orderIds = orderIds;
        this.tradeIds = tradeIds;
    }

    public void submit(Command command) {
        queue.offer(command);
    }

    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (running) {
            try {
                Command cmd = queue.take();
                handle(cmd);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                break;
            } catch (Exception e) {
                // log and continue; production code should isolate poison messages
                e.printStackTrace();
            }
        }
    }

    private void handle(Command cmd) {
        switch (cmd) {
            case NewOrderCommand noc -> onNewOrder(noc);
            case CancelOrderCommand coc -> onCancel(coc);
        }
    }

    private void onNewOrder(NewOrderCommand cmd) {
        OrderBook book = books.computeIfAbsent(cmd.request().instrument(), k -> new OrderBook());
        Order order = new Order(
            orderIds.next(),
            cmd.request().clientId(),
            cmd.request().instrument(),
            cmd.request().side(),
            cmd.request().orderType(),
            cmd.request().tif(),
            cmd.request().quantity(),
            cmd.request().price(),
            System.nanoTime(),
            cmd.request().clientOrderId()
        );

        List<Trade> trades = book.add(order, tradeIds);

        // publish events: accepted, partial fill, filled, booked, etc.
        System.out.println("Accepted order " + order.orderId + ", trades=" + trades.size());
    }

    private void onCancel(CancelOrderCommand cmd) {
        OrderBook book = books.get(cmd.instrument());
        boolean canceled = book != null && book.cancel(cmd.orderId());
        System.out.println("Cancel " + cmd.orderId() + " => " + canceled);
    }

    public void stop() {
        running = false;
    }
}
```

