# 11. Risk checks

Initial pre-trade risk checks should be synchronous and cheap.

Examples:
- Max order size
- Price collars
- Fat-finger checks
- Client enabled/disabled
- Instrument tradable
- Position/notional limits
- Duplicate client order ID detection

## Example risk interface
```java
public interface RiskChecker {
    RiskResult check(NewOrderRequest request);
}

public record RiskResult(boolean allowed, String reason) {
    public static RiskResult allow() { return new RiskResult(true, "OK"); }
    public static RiskResult reject(String reason) { return new RiskResult(false, reason); }
}
```

## Simple implementation
```java
import java.util.Set;

public final class BasicRiskChecker implements RiskChecker {
    private final Set<String> enabledClients;
    private final long maxOrderQty;

    public BasicRiskChecker(Set<String> enabledClients, long maxOrderQty) {
        this.enabledClients = enabledClients;
        this.maxOrderQty = maxOrderQty;
    }

    @Override
    public RiskResult check(NewOrderRequest request) {
        if (!enabledClients.contains(request.clientId())) {
            return RiskResult.reject("CLIENT_DISABLED");
        }
        if (request.quantity() <= 0) {
            return RiskResult.reject("INVALID_QTY");
        }
        if (request.orderType() == OrderType.LIMIT && request.price() <= 0) {
            return RiskResult.reject("INVALID_PRICE");
        }
        if (request.quantity() > maxOrderQty) {
            return RiskResult.reject("MAX_QTY_EXCEEDED");
        }
        return RiskResult.allow();
    }
}
```

