## Single-file example

```java
import com.lmax.disruptor.*;
import com.lmax.disruptor.dsl.Disruptor;
import com.lmax.disruptor.dsl.ProducerType;

import java.util.Map;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.LongAdder;

public class HighFrequencyMessagingSystem {

    // -----------------------------
    // Message model
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class Message {
        long id;
        long createdAtNanos;
        String destination;
        byte[] payload;

        public void set(long id, long createdAtNanos, String destination, byte[] payload) {
            this.id = id;
            this.createdAtNanos = createdAtNanos;
            this.destination = destination;
            this.payload = payload;
        }

        public void clear() {
            this.id = 0;
            this.createdAtNanos = 0;
            this.destination = null;
            this.payload = null;
        }
    }

    public static final class MessageEventFactory implements EventFactory<Message> {
        @Override
        public Message newInstance() {
            return new Message();
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Metrics
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class Metrics {
        private final LongAdder published = new LongAdder();
        private final LongAdder routed = new LongAdder();
        private final LongAdder dropped = new LongAdder();
        private final LongAdder failed = new LongAdder();

        private final LongAdder totalLatencyNanos = new LongAdder();
        private final LongAdder maxLatencyNanos = new LongAdder();

        public void markPublished() {
            published.increment();
        }

        public void markRouted(long latencyNanos) {
            routed.increment();
            totalLatencyNanos.add(latencyNanos);
            updateMax(maxLatencyNanos, latencyNanos);
        }

        public void markDropped() {
            dropped.increment();
        }

        public void markFailed() {
            failed.increment();
        }

        public long getPublished() {
            return published.sum();
        }

        public long getRouted() {
            return routed.sum();
        }

        public long getDropped() {
            return dropped.sum();
        }

        public long getFailed() {
            return failed.sum();
        }

        public long getAvgLatencyNanos() {
            long count = routed.sum();
            return count == 0 ? 0 : totalLatencyNanos.sum() / count;
        }

        public long getMaxLatencyNanos() {
            return maxLatencyNanos.sum();
        }

        private void updateMax(LongAdder maxHolder, long value) {
            synchronized (maxHolder) {
                long current = maxHolder.sum();
                if (value > current) {
                    maxHolder.reset();
                    maxHolder.add(value);
                }
            }
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Destination handler interface
    // -----------------------------
    public interface DestinationHandler {
        void onMessage(Message message) throws Exception;
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Router
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class MessageRouter implements EventHandler<Message> {
        private final Map<String, DestinationHandler> handlers;
        private final Metrics metrics;

        public MessageRouter(Map<String, DestinationHandler> handlers, Metrics metrics) {
            this.handlers = handlers;
            this.metrics = metrics;
        }

        @Override
        public void onEvent(Message event, long sequence, boolean endOfBatch) {
            long now = System.nanoTime();
            long latency = now - event.createdAtNanos;

            try {
                DestinationHandler handler = handlers.get(event.destination);
                if (handler == null) {
                    metrics.markDropped();
                    return;
                }

                handler.onMessage(event);
                metrics.markRouted(latency);
            } catch (Exception e) {
                metrics.markFailed();
            } finally {
                event.clear();
            }
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Publisher
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class Publisher {
        private final RingBuffer<Message> ringBuffer;
        private final Metrics metrics;

        public Publisher(RingBuffer<Message> ringBuffer, Metrics metrics) {
            this.ringBuffer = ringBuffer;
            this.metrics = metrics;
        }

        public boolean publish(long id, String destination, byte[] payload) {
            try {
                long sequence = ringBuffer.tryNext();
                try {
                    Message event = ringBuffer.get(sequence);
                    event.set(id, System.nanoTime(), destination, payload);
                } finally {
                    ringBuffer.publish(sequence);
                }
                metrics.markPublished();
                return true;
            } catch (InsufficientCapacityException e) {
                metrics.markDropped();
                return false;
            }
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Example destination handlers
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class PrintHandler implements DestinationHandler {
        private final String name;

        public PrintHandler(String name) {
            this.name = name;
        }

        @Override
        public void onMessage(Message message) {
            // In a real HFT/low-latency system, avoid println in hot path.
            // This is just a placeholder.
            if (message.id % 1_000_000 == 0) {
                System.out.println("[" + name + "] processed message id=" + message.id);
            }
        }
    }

    public static final class BlackholeHandler implements DestinationHandler {
        @Override
        public void onMessage(Message message) {
            // Simulate ultra-fast processing
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Metrics reporter
    // -----------------------------
    public static final class MetricsReporter implements Runnable {
        private final Metrics metrics;
        private long lastPublished = 0;
        private long lastRouted = 0;
        private long lastDropped = 0;
        private long lastFailed = 0;

        public MetricsReporter(Metrics metrics) {
            this.metrics = metrics;
        }

        @Override
        public void run() {
            long pub = metrics.getPublished();
            long routed = metrics.getRouted();
            long dropped = metrics.getDropped();
            long failed = metrics.getFailed();

            long pubDelta = pub - lastPublished;
            long routedDelta = routed - lastRouted;
            long droppedDelta = dropped - lastDropped;
            long failedDelta = failed - lastFailed;

            lastPublished = pub;
            lastRouted = routed;
            lastDropped = dropped;
            lastFailed = failed;

            System.out.printf(
                "TPS pub=%d routed=%d dropped=%d failed=%d avgLat=%.3f us maxLat=%.3f us%n",
                pubDelta,
                routedDelta,
                droppedDelta,
                failedDelta,
                metrics.getAvgLatencyNanos() / 1_000.0,
                metrics.getMaxLatencyNanos() / 1_000.0
            );
        }
    }

    // -----------------------------
    // Main
    // -----------------------------
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        int ringBufferSize = 1024 * 1024; // power of 2
        Metrics metrics = new Metrics();

        ThreadFactory threadFactory = r -> {
            Thread t = new Thread(r);
            t.setName("router-thread");
            t.setDaemon(true);
            return t;
        };

        Disruptor<Message> disruptor = new Disruptor<>(
            new MessageEventFactory(),
            ringBufferSize,
            threadFactory,
            ProducerType.MULTI,
            new BusySpinWaitStrategy()
        );

        Map<String, DestinationHandler> handlers = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
        handlers.put("orders", new BlackholeHandler());
        handlers.put("trades", new BlackholeHandler());
        handlers.put("audit", new PrintHandler("audit"));

        disruptor.handleEventsWith(new MessageRouter(handlers, metrics));
        disruptor.setDefaultExceptionHandler(new ExceptionHandler<Message>() {
            @Override
            public void handleEventException(Throwable ex, long sequence, Message event) {
                metrics.markFailed();
            }

            @Override
            public void handleOnStartException(Throwable ex) {
                ex.printStackTrace();
            }

            @Override
            public void handleOnShutdownException(Throwable ex) {
                ex.printStackTrace();
            }
        });

        disruptor.start();

        RingBuffer<Message> ringBuffer = disruptor.getRingBuffer();
        Publisher publisher = new Publisher(ringBuffer, metrics);

        ScheduledExecutorService reporter = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
        reporter.scheduleAtFixedRate(new MetricsReporter(metrics), 1, 1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

        int producerThreads = Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors();
        ExecutorService producers = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(producerThreads);

        for (int i = 0; i < producerThreads; i++) {
            final int producerId = i;
            producers.submit(() -> {
                long msgId = producerId * 1_000_000_000L;
                byte[] payload = new byte[128];

                while (!Thread.currentThread().isInterrupted()) {
                    String destination;
                    long mod = msgId % 3;
                    if (mod == 0) destination = "orders";
                    else if (mod == 1) destination = "trades";
                    else destination = "audit";

                    publisher.publish(msgId, destination, payload);
                    msgId++;
                }
            });
        }

        Runtime.getRuntime().addShutdownHook(new Thread(() -> {
            producers.shutdownNow();
            reporter.shutdownNow();
            disruptor.shutdown();
        }));

        // Keep running
        Thread.currentThread().join();
    }
}
```

---

# What this does

## Fast path
- Producers publish messages into a **Disruptor ring buffer**
- A router consumes messages with very low coordination overhead
- Messages are dispatched by `destination`

## Latency monitoring
Each message gets:
- `createdAtNanos = System.nanoTime()` at publish time

At consume time:
- `latency = now - createdAtNanos`

Metrics tracked:
- published
- routed
- dropped
- failed
- average latency
- max latency

## Backpressure behavior
This line:

```java
long sequence = ringBuffer.tryNext();
```

makes publishing **non-blocking**.

If the ring buffer is full:
- `InsufficientCapacityException` is thrown
- message is counted as dropped

That is often preferable in high-frequency systems where blocking is worse than dropping.

---

# Production improvements you likely want

## 1. Avoid `String` routing keys in hot path
Use integer route IDs instead:

```java
int routeId;
```

Then route via array lookup instead of `Map<String, ...>`.

---

## 2. Add percentile latency tracking
Average latency is not enough. You usually want:
- p50
- p95
- p99
- p99.9

You can integrate:
- **HdrHistogram**
- **Micrometer**
- **Prometheus**

Example dependency:

```xml
<dependency>
    <groupId>org.hdrhistogram</groupId>
    <artifactId>HdrHistogram</artifactId>
    <version>2.1.12</version>
</dependency>
```

---

## 3. Use object-free payload handling
To reduce GC pressure:
- preallocate buffers
- use direct `ByteBuffer`
- reuse message objects
- avoid `String`
- avoid allocating `byte[]` per message

---

## 4. Pin threads / tune CPU affinity
For true ultra-low latency:
- isolate cores
- pin producer/consumer threads
- disable CPU frequency scaling
- tune JVM GC

---

## 5. Multi-stage pipeline
Real systems often separate:
- ingress
- validation
- routing
- delivery
- persistence
- metrics

Disruptor supports chained handlers.

---

## 6. Add per-route queues
If one destination is slower than others, you may want:
- one ingress ring buffer
- one ring buffer per destination
- dedicated consumers per destination

This prevents a slow route from affecting all traffic.

---

# Example of lower-GC route ID optimization

Instead of:

```java
String destination
```

use:

```java
int routeId
```

and:

```java
DestinationHandler[] handlers = new DestinationHandler[MAX_ROUTES];
DestinationHandler handler = handlers[event.routeId];
```

That is much faster than a concurrent map lookup.

---

# When this design is appropriate

Use this when:
- you need **extremely high throughput**
- routing is mostly **in-memory**
- you care about **microsecond-level latency**
- you can tolerate **best-effort/drop-on-overload** behavior

Not ideal when:
- you need durable delivery guarantees
- messages must survive process crashes
- you need cross-machine distributed routing without another transport layer

For distributed durability, pair this with:
- **Kafka**
- **NATS**
- **Aeron**
- **Chronicle Queue**
- **Redis Streams**
- **Pulsar**

