# 3. Message model

Use a reusable event object to avoid allocations.

```java
package hfmsg;

public final class MessageEvent {
    long messageId;
    long createdNanoTime;
    long ingressNanoTime;
    long routedNanoTime;

    int topicId;
    int partitionKey;
    int payloadLength;

    byte[] payload;

    public MessageEvent() {
        this.payload = new byte[1024]; // fixed-size for demo; use pooled buffers in production
    }

    public void set(
            long messageId,
            long createdNanoTime,
            int topicId,
            int partitionKey,
            byte[] srcPayload,
            int payloadLength) {

        this.messageId = messageId;
        this.createdNanoTime = createdNanoTime;
        this.ingressNanoTime = System.nanoTime();
        this.routedNanoTime = 0L;
        this.topicId = topicId;
        this.partitionKey = partitionKey;
        this.payloadLength = payloadLength;

        System.arraycopy(srcPayload, 0, this.payload, 0, payloadLength);
    }

    public void clear() {
        this.messageId = 0L;
        this.createdNanoTime = 0L;
        this.ingressNanoTime = 0L;
        this.routedNanoTime = 0L;
        this.topicId = 0;
        this.partitionKey = 0;
        this.payloadLength = 0;
    }
}
```

