## Example: bounded parallel processing

If parsing is cheap but record processing is expensive, use a bounded channel so memory stays controlled.

Sketch:

```rust
use std::sync::mpsc::sync_channel;
use std::thread;

// bounded queue prevents unbounded memory growth
let (tx, rx) = sync_channel::<Vec<u8>>(1024);

let worker = thread::spawn(move || {
    while let Ok(line) = rx.recv() {
        // process line
        let _ = line;
    }
});

parser.parse_lines(|line| {
    tx.send(line.to_vec())
        .map_err(|_| io::Error::new(io::ErrorKind::BrokenPipe, "worker disconnected"))?;
    Ok(())
})?;

drop(tx);
worker.join().unwrap();
```

This does allocate per queued record, but keeps total memory bounded.

