## Higher-throughput variant using `fill_buf`

If you want even lower overhead, you can parse directly from the reader’s internal buffer and scan bytes manually. This reduces line-copying overhead from `read_until`.

Here is a more advanced version for newline-delimited records:

```rust
use std::fs::File;
use std::io::{self, BufRead, BufReader};

pub fn parse_stream_fill_buf<R, F>(
    mut reader: R,
    mut on_line: F,
) -> io::Result<()>
where
    R: BufRead,
    F: FnMut(&[u8]) -> io::Result<()>,
{
    let mut carry = Vec::<u8>::new();

    loop {
        let buf = reader.fill_buf()?;
        if buf.is_empty() {
            if !carry.is_empty() {
                on_line(&carry)?;
            }
            break;
        }

        let mut start = 0;
        for i in 0..buf.len() {
            if buf[i] == b'\n' {
                if carry.is_empty() {
                    let mut line = &buf[start..i];
                    if line.ends_with(b"\r") {
                        line = &line[..line.len() - 1];
                    }
                    on_line(line)?;
                } else {
                    carry.extend_from_slice(&buf[start..i]);
                    if carry.ends_with(b"\r") {
                        carry.pop();
                    }
                    on_line(&carry)?;
                    carry.clear();
                }
                start = i + 1;
            }
        }

        if start < buf.len() {
            carry.extend_from_slice(&buf[start..]);
        }

        let consumed = buf.len();
        reader.consume(consumed);
    }

    Ok(())
}

fn main() -> io::Result<()> {
    let file = File::open("large_input.csv")?;
    let reader = BufReader::with_capacity(1024 * 1024, file);

    let mut count = 0u64;

    parse_stream_fill_buf(reader, |line| {
        count += 1;

        // Example: split manually without allocation
        let mut field_count = 1;
        for &b in line {
            if b == b',' {
                field_count += 1;
            }
        }

        if count % 1_000_000 == 0 {
            eprintln!("processed {} records", count);
        }

        let _ = field_count;
        Ok(())
    })?;

    println!("total records={}", count);
    Ok(())
}
```

