## Memory-constrained design notes

Why this is memory-friendly:
- No heap allocation (`malloc`, `calloc`, etc.)
- Fixed-size stack buffers
- No directory scanning
- No parsing of large config files
- No threads
- No in-memory log buffering
- Constant memory footprint

Approximate memory behavior:
