This is a practical minimal implementation, not a full `logrotate` replacement.

## Features

- Monitors one log file
- Rotates when file size exceeds a threshold
- Renames:
  - `app.log.4 -> app.log.5`
  - `app.log.3 -> app.log.4`
  - ...
  - `app.log -> app.log.1`
- Keeps `N` rotated files
- Runs as a daemon
- Uses very little memory
