## Notes on memory constraints

This implementation is memory-constrained because it:

- allocates all buffers statically/on stack
- uses small fixed buffers
- does not read log contents into memory
- relies on filesystem rename operations instead of copying data

---

## Important limitation

If the application writing the log keeps the file descriptor open, renaming the file alone may not make it start writing to the new log file automatically. In that case, the writer must:

- reopen the log on `SIGHUP`, or
- use a logging framework that supports log rotation

This daemon rotates filenames, but cannot force another process to reopen its log unless you add signaling support.

