## Important limitation
If the writer process keeps the log file open across rotation, it may continue writing to the renamed file instead of the new one. This is standard behavior for simple rename-based rotation.

Typical solutions:
- signal the writer to reopen logs
- use copy-truncate instead of rename
- integrate with the application

