## Optional strict memory limit at runtime

On Linux/Unix, you can enforce memory caps with `setrlimit()`:

Add this function:

```c
#include <sys/resource.h>

static int set_memory_limit(size_t bytes) {
    struct rlimit rl;
    rl.rlim_cur = bytes;
    rl.rlim_max = bytes;
    return setrlimit(RLIMIT_AS, &rl);
}
```

Then call it early in `main()`:

```c
if (set_memory_limit(8 * 1024 * 1024) < 0) {
    perror("setrlimit");
    return 1;
}
```

For even tighter control, also limit data segment:

```c
static int set_data_limit(size_t bytes) {
    struct rlimit rl;
    rl.rlim_cur = bytes;
    rl.rlim_max = bytes;
    return setrlimit(RLIMIT_DATA, &rl);
}
```

