## Performance notes

To make this truly high-performance in production:

- prefer **Unix domain sockets** over TCP if local-only
- reduce refresh scope if you don’t need full process enumeration every tick
- split fast-path metrics and slower process scans into separate intervals
- export Prometheus text format if integrating with standard monitoring
- use lock-free snapshots or `arc-swap` if read contention becomes significant
- pin polling cadence carefully; 250–1000 ms is usually enough
- avoid spawning shell commands for metrics collection
- run with least privilege

