# Important bug fix to apply immediately

There is one logic issue in the initial insertion/update path.

This part:

```rust
let entry = flows
    .entry(parsed.flow_key)
    .or_insert_with(|| FlowStats::new(now, parsed.ip_total_len));

if entry.packets > 1 || entry.bytes > parsed.ip_total_len as u64 {
    entry.update(now, parsed.ip_total_len);
}
```

is awkward and can undercount or behave unexpectedly.

Replace it with this cleaner version:

```rust
use std::collections::hash_map::Entry;
```

Actually, since you're using `AHashMap`, use:

```rust
match flows.entry(parsed.flow_key) {
    ahash::hash_map::Entry::Occupied(mut occ) => {
        let entry = occ.get_mut();
        entry.update(now, parsed.ip_total_len);

        if let Some(flags) = parsed.tcp_flags {
            if flags & 0x02 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_syn += 1;
            }
            if flags & 0x01 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_fin += 1;
            }
            if flags & 0x04 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_rst += 1;
            }
        }
    }
    ahash::hash_map::Entry::Vacant(vac) => {
        let mut entry = FlowStats::new(now, parsed.ip_total_len);

        if let Some(flags) = parsed.tcp_flags {
            if flags & 0x02 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_syn += 1;
            }
            if flags & 0x01 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_fin += 1;
            }
            if flags & 0x04 != 0 {
                entry.tcp_rst += 1;
            }
        }

        vac.insert(entry);
    }
}
```

So the packet-processing section should use that instead.

