# Example with simple exponential filter

If you prefer an IIR filter instead of a moving average, use this:

```c
static float filtered_adc = 0.0f;
static bool filter_initialized = false;

static uint16_t Filter_ADC(uint16_t raw)
{
    const float alpha = 0.2f;  // 0..1, lower = more smoothing

    if (!filter_initialized)
    {
        filtered_adc = (float)raw;
        filter_initialized = true;
    }
    else
    {
        filtered_adc = alpha * raw + (1.0f - alpha) * filtered_adc;
    }

    return (uint16_t)filtered_adc;
}
```

Then in `ProcessSensor()`:

```c
static void ProcessSensor(uint8_t adc_channel, SensorData_t *data)
{
    uint16_t raw = ADC_ReadChannel(adc_channel);
    uint16_t filtered = Filter_ADC(raw);

    float voltage = ADC_ToVoltage(filtered);
    float processed = Voltage_ToEngineeringUnits(voltage);

    data->raw_adc = filtered;
    data->voltage = voltage;
    data->processed_value = processed;
    data->alarm_high = (processed > SENSOR_HIGH_THRESHOLD);
    data->alarm_low = (processed < SENSOR_LOW_THRESHOLD);
}
```

