# Example with hysteresis for alarms

To avoid alarm chatter near thresholds:

```c
#define HIGH_THRESHOLD_ON   80.0f
#define HIGH_THRESHOLD_OFF  75.0f
#define LOW_THRESHOLD_ON    10.0f
#define LOW_THRESHOLD_OFF   15.0f

static void Sensor_HandleThresholds(void)
{
    if (!sensor.alarm_high && sensor.physical_value > HIGH_THRESHOLD_ON)
        sensor.alarm_high = true;
    else if (sensor.alarm_high && sensor.physical_value < HIGH_THRESHOLD_OFF)
        sensor.alarm_high = false;

    if (!sensor.alarm_low && sensor.physical_value < LOW_THRESHOLD_ON)
        sensor.alarm_low = true;
    else if (sensor.alarm_low && sensor.physical_value > LOW_THRESHOLD_OFF)
        sensor.alarm_low = false;
}
```

Then call `Sensor_HandleThresholds()` after computing `physical_value`.

