## Example with hysteresis for alarms

To avoid alarm chatter near thresholds, use hysteresis:

```c
#define HIGH_THRESHOLD_ON   80.0f
#define HIGH_THRESHOLD_OFF  75.0f
#define LOW_THRESHOLD_ON    10.0f
#define LOW_THRESHOLD_OFF   15.0f

static void Check_Alarms(SensorData_t *data)
{
    static bool high_alarm = false;
    static bool low_alarm = false;

    if (!high_alarm && data->value > HIGH_THRESHOLD_ON)
        high_alarm = true;
    else if (high_alarm && data->value < HIGH_THRESHOLD_OFF)
        high_alarm = false;

    if (!low_alarm && data->value < LOW_THRESHOLD_ON)
        low_alarm = true;
    else if (low_alarm && data->value > LOW_THRESHOLD_OFF)
        low_alarm = false;

    data->alarm_high = high_alarm;
    data->alarm_low = low_alarm;
}
```

