# 7. Example for a Digital Sensor Instead

If your sensor is I2C/SPI rather than analog ADC, the structure stays the same. Only `Sensor_ReadAndProcess()` changes.

Example concept:

```c
bool I2C_ReadSensorRegisters(uint8_t devAddr, uint8_t reg, uint8_t *data, uint8_t len);

static void Sensor_ReadAndProcess(SensorData_t *data, MovingAverageFilter_t *filter)
{
    uint8_t rx[2];
    if (I2C_ReadSensorRegisters(0x48, 0x00, rx, 2))
    {
        uint16_t raw = ((uint16_t)rx[0] << 8) | rx[1];
        data->raw = raw;
        data->voltage = (float)raw * 0.001f; /* example conversion */
        data->filtered_voltage = MovingAverage_Update(filter, data->voltage);
        data->alarm_high = (data->filtered_voltage > SENSOR_HIGH_THRESHOLD_V);
        data->alarm_low  = (data->filtered_voltage < SENSOR_LOW_THRESHOLD_V);
    }
}
