Below is a compact embedded-style C implementation of an accelerometer anomaly-detection pipeline suitable for a microcontroller.

It includes:

- 3-axis accelerometer sample handling
- Magnitude estimation
- Low-pass baseline tracking
- High-pass residual extraction
- Rolling noise estimate
- Z-score style anomaly detection
- Consecutive-hit debounce
- Optional cooldown to avoid repeated triggers

You can adapt it for bare metal, RTOS, Arduino, or STM32 projects.

