# 10. Minimal fixed-point-friendly variant idea

If you want to avoid `sqrtf`, use squared magnitude:

```c
mag2 = ax*ax + ay*ay + az*az;
score = abs(mag2 - mean2);
if (score > threshold2) anomaly = true;
```

This is less statistically clean than z-score, but often good enough for shock/event detection on small MCUs.

