## Slightly more robust variant idea

Instead of updating stats with every sample, you may want to **freeze baseline updates during anomalies**, so large events do not immediately contaminate the baseline.

That change would look like:

```c
if (!anomaly) {
    running_stats_update(&p->stats, mag);
}
```

This is often a better default for anomaly detection.

