## Even lighter alternative: IIR filter

If memory is very tight, replace the moving average with a first-order IIR filter:

```c
typedef struct {
    int32_t value; /* fixed-point scaled by 256 */
} IIRFilter;

static void iir_init(IIRFilter *f, int16_t initial) {
    f->value = ((int32_t)initial) << 8;
}

static int16_t iir_update(IIRFilter *f, int16_t sample) {
    /* alpha = 1/8 */
    int32_t target = ((int32_t)sample) << 8;
    f->value += (target - f->value) >> 3;
    return (int16_t)(f->value >> 8);
}
```

This uses less RAM and is often better for tiny MCUs.

