## Even lighter alternative

If memory is extremely tight, replace the moving average with an exponential moving average:

```c
typedef struct {
    uint16_t value;
    bool initialized;
} EmaFilter;

static uint16_t ema_update(EmaFilter *f, uint16_t sample) {
    if (!f->initialized) {
        f->value = sample;
        f->initialized = true;
    } else {
        /* alpha = 1/4 */
        f->value = (uint16_t)((3 * f->value + sample) / 4);
    }
    return f->value;
}
```

This reduces memory from `FILTER_WINDOW * sizeof(uint16_t)` per sensor to just a few bytes.

