# 16. Recommended next upgrade: simple ground collision

A very useful next step is adding a basic static plane collision so dynamic bodies don’t fall forever.

For example, inside `SimulateStep()` after integration:

```cpp
void PhysicsWorld::SimulateStep(float dt)
{
    for (auto& [handle, body] : m_bodies)
    {
        body->Integrate(dt, m_gravity);

        if (body->GetType() == BodyType::Dynamic)
        {
            Transform t = body->GetTransform();
            Vec3 v = body->GetLinearVelocity();

            // Simple ground plane at y = 0
            if (t.position.y < 0.0f)
            {
                t.position.y = 0.0f;
                if (v.y < 0.0f)
                {
                    v.y = 0.0f;
                }

                body->SetTransform(t);
                body->SetLinearVelocity(v);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

That gives immediate visible behavior.

