# 12. Example fixed timestep upgrade

Here’s a simple improvement for the subsystem:

In header:

```cpp
private:
    float TimeAccumulator = 0.0f;
    float FixedTimeStep = 1.0f / 60.0f;
```

In `Tick`:

```cpp
void UCustomPhysicsWorldSubsystem::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    TimeAccumulator += DeltaTime;

    while (TimeAccumulator >= FixedTimeStep)
    {
        for (int32 i = Bodies.Num() - 1; i >= 0; --i)
        {
            UCustomPhysicsBodyComponent* Body = Bodies[i];
            if (!IsValid(Body) || !IsValid(Body->GetOwner()))
            {
                Bodies.RemoveAt(i);
                continue;
            }

            if (!Body->bSimulate)
            {
                continue;
            }

            SimulateBody(Body, FixedTimeStep);
        }

        TimeAccumulator -= FixedTimeStep;
    }
}
```

This makes the simulation more stable.

