# Important note about ticking

Right now, the component only **reads** body state. The world still needs to be stepped each frame.

You can do that in several ways:

- Engine subsystem tick
- World subsystem
- Module-level ticker
- Dedicated physics scene hook

For an initial implementation, a simple ticker is enough.

## Example Unreal ticker hookup

Add to module header:

```cpp
#include "Containers/Ticker.h"
```

```cpp
private:
    bool Tick(float DeltaTime);
    FTSTicker::FDelegateHandle TickHandle;
```

Then in module cpp:

```cpp
void FCustomPhysicsPluginModule::StartupModule()
{
    PhysicsWorld = MakeUnique<FPhysicsWorld>();
    TickHandle = FTSTicker::GetCoreTicker().AddTicker(
        FTickerDelegate::CreateRaw(this, &FCustomPhysicsPluginModule::Tick));
}

void FCustomPhysicsPluginModule::ShutdownModule()
{
    FTSTicker::GetCoreTicker().RemoveTicker(TickHandle);
    PhysicsWorld.Reset();
}

bool FCustomPhysicsPluginModule::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    if (PhysicsWorld)
    {
        PhysicsWorld->StepSimulation(DeltaTime);
    }
    return true;
}
