# 12. Example: fixed timestep upgrade sketch

Here’s a minimal direction for improving the subsystem:

Add members:

```cpp
float FixedTimeStep = 1.0f / 60.0f;
float TimeAccumulator = 0.0f;
```

Then in `Tick`:

```cpp
void UCustomPhysicsSubsystem::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    if (DeltaTime <= KINDA_SMALL_NUMBER)
    {
        return;
    }

    TimeAccumulator += DeltaTime;

    while (TimeAccumulator >= FixedTimeStep)
    {
        for (int32 i = Bodies.Num() - 1; i >= 0; --i)
        {
            FCustomPhysicsBodyEntry& Body = Bodies[i];

            if (!IsValid(Body.Component))
            {
                Bodies.RemoveAtSwap(i);
                continue;
            }

            SimulateBody(Body, FixedTimeStep);
        }

        TimeAccumulator -= FixedTimeStep;
    }
}
```

This will make the simulation more stable.

