# 11. Example: fixed timestep improvement

A better simulation pattern is fixed-step updates.

Add to subsystem header:

```cpp
private:
    float Accumulator = 0.0f;
    float FixedTimeStep = 1.0f / 60.0f;

    void StepSimulation(float StepTime);
```

Update tick:

```cpp
void UCustomPhysicsSubsystem::Tick(float DeltaTime)
{
    Accumulator += DeltaTime;

    while (Accumulator >= FixedTimeStep)
    {
        StepSimulation(FixedTimeStep);
        Accumulator -= FixedTimeStep;
    }
}
```

Add:

```cpp
void UCustomPhysicsSubsystem::StepSimulation(float StepTime)
{
    for (TPair<int32, FSimplePhysicsBody>& Pair : Bodies)
    {
        SimulateBody(Pair.Value, StepTime);
    }
}
```

This gives more stable behavior than variable timestep integration.

