# 13. Important commercial-engine integration note

For a real commercial engine plugin, you usually should **not** expose STL-heavy C++ classes directly across the DLL boundary unless the engine guarantees ABI compatibility.

A safer production interface would export C-style functions like:

```cpp
extern "C" {
    bool Physics_Initialize();
    void Physics_Shutdown();
    int Physics_CreateSphere(float mass, float x, float y, float z, float radius);
    void Physics_Tick(float dt);
}
```

or use the engine’s own reflection/module system.

