# 16. Important production considerations

This implementation is a good starting point, but a large financial institution will require more before production:

## Security
- OAuth2 / mTLS
- Role-based access control
- Request signing
- Encryption at rest and in transit
- Secrets management via Vault/KMS

## Compliance
- Full audit trail
- PII/tokenization strategy
- AML/sanctions/fraud screening
- SOX/PCI/GDPR controls depending on scope

## Reliability
- Outbox pattern for event publication
- Message-driven asynchronous processing
- Retry policies with backoff
- Circuit breakers for downstream systems
- Dead-letter queues

## Data integrity
- Strong idempotency semantics
- Immutable ledger entries instead of only status mutation
- Double-entry accounting integration
- Reconciliation jobs
- Exactly-once or effectively-once processing strategy

## Operational maturity
- Structured logging
- Distributed tracing
- Metrics and SLAs
- Blue/green or canary deployment
- Database migration tooling like Flyway/Liquibase

## Domain sophistication
- Cutoff windows
- Holiday calendars
- FX conversion
- Fees
- Multi-step approvals
- Payment repair workflows
- Returns, reversals, and cancellations

