# 1. High-level architecture

A realistic payment processing service should include:

- API layer
  - receive payment requests
  - validate input
  - enforce idempotency
- Application/service layer
  - orchestrate payment lifecycle
  - call fraud/risk/compliance checks
  - reserve/debit funds
  - persist state transitions
- Domain layer
  - payment entity
  - status model
  - business rules
- Persistence layer
  - payment records
  - audit trail
  - idempotency records
- Integration layer
  - core banking / ledger
  - AML/KYC/fraud systems
  - notification/event bus

Typical payment lifecycle:

- RECEIVED
- VALIDATED
- PROCESSING
- COMPLETED
- FAILED
- REJECTED

