# 9. Infrastructure repository

For an initial implementation, I’ll provide an in-memory repository. In a real enterprise deployment, this would be replaced by PostgreSQL, Oracle, SQL Server, or an internal persistence adapter.

## `src/infrastructure/db/in-memory-customer-repository.ts`

```ts
import type { CustomerRepository } from "../../domain/customer/customer-repository.js";
import type { Customer, CustomerId } from "../../domain/customer/customer.js";

export class InMemoryCustomerRepository implements CustomerRepository {
  private readonly customers = new Map<CustomerId, Customer>();

  public constructor(seed?: readonly Customer[]) {
    for (const customer of seed ?? []) {
      this.customers.set(customer.id, customer);
    }
  }

  public async findById(id: CustomerId): Promise<Customer | null> {
    return this.customers.get(id) ?? null;
  }

  public async findAll(): Promise<readonly Customer[]> {
    return [...this.customers.values()];
  }

  public async save(customer: Customer): Promise<Customer> {
    this.customers.set(customer.id, customer);
    return customer;
  }
}
```

